cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. It has not been peer reviewed."
title: "linear-a-b: a statistical review of how the Aegean scripts are read"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Howe
    given-names: Ru
    email: ru@stornaway.io
repository-code: "https://github.com/ruhowe/linear-a-b"
url: "https://github.com/ruhowe/linear-a-b"
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  Tests of the methods used to read Linear A and Linear B, run against controls, with
  Linear B as the control script where the answer is known: dictionary matching against
  wrong real languages, Alice Kober's structural method by machine with a measured
  corpus-size floor, place-name evidence for the transferred sound values under a
  permutation null, and a Linear B restoration benchmark against its frequency floor.
  Findings are dated and versioned in FINDINGS.md. Code is MIT; everything else is
  CC BY-SA 4.0 (see LICENSE.md). Produced with Claude Code under the author's direction;
  not reviewed by any specialist.
keywords:
  - Linear A
  - Linear B
  - Aegean scripts
  - decipherment
  - Mycenaean Greek
  - statistical controls
